      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, showing Elias choosing peace over the exhausting role of \"the hero\" is often the most powerful way to reflect the truth of profound burnout. His story resonates not because he conquers the world, but because he finally surrenders the need to be understood by it. Sometimes the most impactful ending is one where a character stops performing pain and simply walks away into the quiet.",
      "source": "target",
